ames (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Michigan's 10th District is an open seat after Republican John James left to run for governor, and it sits in Republican-leaning territory with a partisan lean of about three points toward the GOP. Christina Hines has raised over $4 million and drawn surrogates including Hakeem Jeffries, Mark Kelly, and Governor Whitmer, while Trump-backed Mike Bouchard Jr. has also raised nearly $3 million. Outside groups have spent heavily on both sides, with more opposing Hines.\n\nPolling is thin and mixed: a Democratic-sponsored August poll showed a tie, while a late-October poll put Bouchard up five. Expert ratings split between Tossup and Lean D, and prediction markets price Hines around 76%. The race looks like a genuine tossup with a modest Democratic edge, and the outcome may hinge on turnout in Macomb County.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6628, "margin": 2.54}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6491, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6831, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6477, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.623, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.5903, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6399, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.6806, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.6694, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7119, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.6799, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.6842, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.6979, "margin": 2.8}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.6212, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.6272, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.6412, "margin": 2.8}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.6477, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.6501, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.6527, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.6567, "margin": 3.0}, {"d